Mail: every spawned job gets a pipe to its parent. The job and every shell under it write
the write end, named to recipes as AMK_MAIL and to a guest through amk_mail_send; the
parent drains the read end while it waits and hands the text over once, through
amk_mail_take, when the job is collected. A job's word to the loop that spawned it is a
write to a descriptor, not a file in a run directory.

